\"__typename\":\"CreditedRoleEdge\"}],\"__typename\":\"CreditedRoleConnection\"},\"episodeCredits\":{\"total\":6,\"yearRange\":{\"year\":2016,\"endYear\":2020,\"__typename\":\"YearRange\"},\"__typename\":\"EpisodeCreditConnection\"},\"__typename\":\"CreditV2\"}],\"__typename\":\"PrincipalCreditsForGrouping\"}],\"crewV2\":[{\"totalCredits\":2,\"grouping\":{\"groupingId\":\"amzn1.imdb.concept.name_credit_group.85198717-6c2d-481e-93a5-47858774bcce\",\"text\":\"Creators\",\"__typename\":\"CreditGrouping\"},\"credits\":[{\"name\":{\"id\":\"nm0329634\",\"nameText\":{\"text\":\"Dan Goor\",\"__typename\":\"NameText\"},\"__typename\":\"Name\"},\"__typename\":\"CreditV2\"},{\"name\":{\"id\":\"nm1321658\",\"nameText\":{\"text\":\"Michael Schur\",\"__typename\":\"NameText\"},\"__typename\":\"Name\"},\"__typename\":\"CreditV2\"}],\"__typename\":\"PrincipalCreditsForGrouping\"}],\"titleText\":{\"text\":\"Brooklyn Nine-Nine\",\"__typename\":\"TitleText\"},\"originalTitleText\":{\"text\":\"Brooklyn Nine-Nine\",\"__typename\":\"TitleText\"},\"canRate\":{\"isRatable\":true,\"__typename\":\"CanRate\"},\"reviews\":{\"total\":988,\"__typename\":\"ReviewsConnection\"},\"aggregateRatingsBreakdown\":{\"histogram\":{\"histogramValues\":[{\"rating\":1,\"voteCount\":4443,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":2,\"voteCount\":1518,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":3,\"voteCount\":1874,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":4,\"voteCount\":2803,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":5677,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":6,\"voteCount\":14449,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":45728,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":105018,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":113049,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"},{\"rating\":10,\"voteCount\":118702,\"__typename\":\"HistogramValues\"}],\"__typename\":\"Histogram\"},\"__typename\":\"AggregateRatingsBreakdown\"},\"featuredReviews\":{\"edges\":[{\"node\":{\"id\":\"rw4022211\",\"author\":{\"userId\":\"ur81737566\",\"username\":{\"text\":\"ansonlam\",\"__typename\":\"UserProfileUsername\"},\"__typename\":\"UserProfile\"},\"summary\":{\"originalText\":\"Delightful show, No Laugh Tracks, Golden Content\",\"__typename\":\"ReviewSummary\"},\"text\":{\"originalText\":{\"plaidHtml\":\"Brooklyn Nine-Nine is definitely one of my favorite ever sitcom. It\\u0026#39;s a show of pure comedy with humorous stories that are naturally delivered by the lovely actors and actresses, but also with a consistent storyline which a lot of sitcoms lack. The other thing I\\u0026#39;ve noticed which makes this show better is the exclusion of laugh tracks. Although, laugh tracks do, to a certain extent, seem to make shows more hilarious and to a point where even if you don\\u0026#39;t understand a joke, you\\u0026#39;d laugh. But no, this show has no cheats like that and amuses viewers with original content.\\nThe show also does not rely on one-liners or simple jokes, and instead, make use of the characters\\u0026#39; personalities and actions to entertain viewers, which is pretty smart. Some might think that entertainment with personalities do not last as they stay the same and eventually people would get tired of them. However, with the ongoing characters development, their personalities and stories are often changing, which makes the show so fresh all the time.\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewText\"},\"title\":{\"id\":\"tt2467372\",\"__typename\":\"Title\"},\"authorRating\":10,\"spoiler\":false,\"__typename\":\"Review\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewEdge\"},{\"node\":{\"id\":\"rw2891599\",\"author\":{\"userId\":\"ur12644957\",\"username\":{\"text\":\"montez7679\",\"__typename\":\"UserProfileUsername\"},\"__typename\":\"UserProfile\"},\"summary\":{\"originalText\":\"I can't understand who wouldn't find this show fantastic\",\"__typename\":\"ReviewSummary\"},\"text\":{\"originalText\":{\"plaidHtml\":\"I respect that different people have different tastes in music, clothes, women, movies etc...but if you are saying that this show is bad I really feel like your sense of humor is lacking. I\\u0026#39;m a detective for one of the largest police departments in the country and I will advise everyone that doesn\\u0026#39;t realize it but this show is closer to how real police go about their day than any of those CSI, or garbage procedural shows. Cops do all that stuff all day...pranking each other, busting balls, trying to have a little fun. The job gets a little heavy sometimes so if we didn\\u0026#39;t have some fun it would be long days. This show is hilarious and perfectly timed retorts by Braugher and Crews are classic. Its the low key lines that make I hilarious...the over the top cheap laughs are somethkng all shows have to do to please the masses...who are stupid. Pay attention to the underlying comedy...its priceless.......\\u0026quot;Terry does love yogurt\\u0026quot;\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewText\"},\"title\":{\"id\":\"tt2467372\",\"__typename\":\"Title\"},\"authorRating\":9,\"spoiler\":false,\"__typename\":\"Review\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewEdge\"},{\"node\":{\"id\":\"rw10555769\",\"author\":{\"userId\":\"ur125721946\",\"username\":{\"text\":\"Didako1221\",\"__typename\":\"UserProfileUsername\"},\"__typename\":\"UserProfile\"},\"summary\":{\"originalText\":\"Started 99, Ended 1\",\"__typename\":\"ReviewSummary\"},\"text\":{\"originalText\":{\"plaidHtml\":\"It started AMAZING!! I\\u0026#39;m talking about the new Friends/Seinfeld level. It had all. Funny, cool, it has been a while. The one I would watch when having a spoiling meal in front of the TV. Too funny sometimes. I fell in love.\\u003cbr/\\u003e\\u003cbr/\\u003eBut. Then the change arrived. They started with the DEI BS on every part of it. Trying to push in the way they see the world and want to force us to follow. Now, if you lived in BK, you know that real life has NOTHING to do with all the BS they spread on us from every screen. Down the block, everyone lives together. And loving it.\\u003cbr/\\u003e\\u003cbr/\\u003eSo Season 1-3.5 - WOW. After it is fans only. And even them I am not sure will agree...\\nJack is the man, LOL.\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewText\"},\"title\":{\"id\":\"tt2467372\",\"__typename\":\"Title\"},\"authorRating\":7,\"spoiler\":false,\"__typename\":\"Review\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewEdge\"},{\"node\":{\"id\":\"rw8492618\",\"author\":{\"userId\":\"ur55640799\",\"username\":{\"text\":\"jack_o_hasanov\",\"__typename\":\"UserProfileUsername\"},\"__typename\":\"UserProfile\"},\"summary\":{\"originalText\":\"Cool Cool Cool Cool\",\"__typename\":\"ReviewSummary\"},\"text\":{\"originalText\":{\"plaidHtml\":\"It was a very good series. It was a fun, funny, excellent character series. Far from sit-com clichés. I can\\u0026#39;t find anything else to write, it was so good and great. The opening scenes were generally very good. I will miss this series. The acting was perfect...Last season was a little weak. There were a few episodes where they were terrible. But the series had an excellent finale. There was one character in the series that I didn\\u0026#39;t like at all, and that was Gina. She was a very annoying and boring character, but Chelsea Perreti played it very well. I had heard the show was funny and entertaining, but I hadn\\u0026#39;t started watching it. But at a time when my work was busy, I started watching it to relax and have fun, and while I was watching this series, I couldn\\u0026#39;t watch any other series.\\u003cbr/\\u003e\\u003cbr/\\u003eCool Cool Cool Cool.\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewText\"},\"title\":{\"id\":\"tt2467372\",\"__typename\":\"Title\"},\"authorRating\":8,\"spoiler\":false,\"__typename\":\"Review\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewEdge\"},{\"node\":{\"id\":\"rw6430390\",\"author\":{\"userId\":\"ur6387867\",\"username\":{\"text\":\"Supermanfan-13\",\"__typename\":\"UserProfileUsername\"},\"__typename\":\"UserProfile\"},\"summary\":{\"originalText\":\"Absolutely Hilarious!\",\"__typename\":\"ReviewSummary\"},\"text\":{\"originalText\":{\"plaidHtml\":\"Brooklyn Nine-Nine is not only laugh out loud funny but it\\u0026#39;s one of the most underrated comedies of all-time! It\\u0026#39;s one of the rare comedies where every character on the show is almost as ridiculously funny as the others. It\\u0026#39;s also one of the rare shows where every season is just as hilarious as the one\\u0026#39;s before it. I can\\u0026#39;t say enough about how hilarious this show really is so just watch it for yourself!\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewText\"},\"title\":{\"id\":\"tt2467372\",\"__typename\":\"Title\"},\"authorRating\":9,\"spoiler\":false,\"__typename\":\"Review\"},\"__typename\":\"ReviewEdge\"}],\"__typename\":\"ReviewsConnection\"},\"reviewSummary\":{\"overall\":{\"medium\":{\"value\":{\"plaidHtml\":\"Reviewers say \\u0026#39;Brooklyn Nine-Nine\\u0026#39; is acclaimed for its humor, ensemble cast, and character growth, especially in early seasons. The show is lauded for its diversity and handling of social issues with a light touch. However, some critics feel later seasons, particularly the final one, became too political and lost comedic charm, shifting focus from entertainment to social commentary. Despite this, \\u0026#39;Brooklyn Nine-Nine\\u0026#39; remains a standout sitcom with memorable moments and a loyal fanbase.\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"LocalizedMarkdown\"},\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewSentimentSection\"},\"themes\":[{\"themeId\":\"binge-worthy\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Binge-worthy\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"POSITIVE\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"},{\"themeId\":\"character-development\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Character development\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"POSITIVE\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"},{\"themeId\":\"chemistry\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Chemistry\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"POSITIVE\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"},{\"themeId\":\"comedic-brilliance\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Comedic brilliance\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"POSITIVE\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"},{\"themeId\":\"identity\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Identity\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"POSITIVE\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"},{\"themeId\":\"rewatchable\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Rewatchable\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"POSITIVE\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"},{\"themeId\":\"social-commentary\",\"label\":{\"value\":\"Social commentary\",\"__typename\":\"LocalizedString\"},\"sentiment\":\"NEUTRAL\",\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewTheme\"}],\"__typename\":\"TitleReviewSummary\"},\"isAdult\":false,\"moreLikeThisTitles\":{\"edges\":[{\"node\":{\"id\":\"tt1442437\",\"titleText\":{\"text\":\"Modern Family\",\"__typename\":\"TitleText\"},\"titleType\":{\"id\":\"tvSeries\",\"text\":\"TV Series\",\"canHaveEpisodes\":true,\"displayableProperty\":{\"value\":{\"plainText\":\"TV Series\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"DisplayableTitleTypeProperty\"},\"__typename\":\"TitleType\"},\"originalTitleText\":{\"text\":\"Modern Family\",\"__typename\":\"TitleText\"},\"primaryImage\":{\"id\":\"rm2302182657\",\"width\":1500,\"height\":2238,\"url\":\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BYzFlOWFjNzQtODViNC00NzgzLThhZmItZTc1N2VlZDgwODUwXkEyXkFqcGc@._V1_.jpg\",\"caption\":{\"plainText\":\"Sofía Vergara, Julie Bowen, Ty Burrell, Jesse Tyler Ferguson, Sarah Hyland, Ed O'Neill, Eric Stonestreet, Beatrice the Dog, Ariel Winter, Nolan Gould, Rico Rodriguez, Reid Ewing, Aubrey Anderson-Emmons, and Jeremy Maguire in Modern Family (2009)\",\"__typename\":\"Markdown\"},\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"releaseYear\":{\"year\":2009,\"endYear\":2020,\"__typename\":\